WEBVTT

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.430
How's it look?

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:04.460
A little crooked on the right.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:05.660
Too far.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:06.980
There! Perfect!

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.540
Now that is quite the sight.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:19.990
It looks good!

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:22.290
Studio...

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:23.790
Eizouken!

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:23.790
<b>Film</b>

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.790
<b>Film</b>

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:30.550
What if we had the logo walk by at the 
beginning of every project, like this?

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.200
I love it!

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.930
We don't even have a project yet.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.340
Oh, there you are, Kanamori—

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.760
Didn't I tell you two not 
to get ahead of yourselves?

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.350
But since we've got a meeting place—

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.940
<b>Film</b>

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.940
It just looks like a random 
sign that says "film."

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.160
A good design is about paying attention 
to the minute details that—

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.210
More importantly...

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:52.470
We need to fix up the building 
and then get to some actual work.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.950
Because otherwise, our little 
group is going to be broken up.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:59.140
Hang on! The eizouken
 only just came together!

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.850
Do you think we have
 all the time in the world?

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:04.920
After a certain someone 
spilled the beans about our

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.940
anime production to a teacher?

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:09.940
No way... I thought you 
convinced him to back down!

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:13.290
Are you getting enough 
oxygen to your brain?

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:16.380
My arguments were all just to get 
him to back off for the time being.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.700
If he thinks about it calmly, 
he'll realize that we don't have a case.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:24.290
My point being, if you don't 
want to take that sign down,

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:26.730
<b>Film</b>

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:26.730
we need to accomplish something.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:32.980
<b>Film</b>

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:37.990
<b><i>Episode 3        Let's Accomplish Something!</i></b>

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.350
<b><i>Keep</i></b>

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.730
<b><i>Your</i></b>

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:37.270
<b><i>Hands</i></b>

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:39.650
<b><i>Off</i></b>

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:50.640
<b><i>Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken!</i></b>

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:58.850
<b><i>Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken!</i></b>

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:05.990
It's time to begin the briefing 
for our repairs of the club room.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:08.350
A lack of suitable seriousness 
will not be tolerated!

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:09.210
Okay!

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.250
Kanamori, if you could get us started.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.500
The phrase "pure profit" speaks to the

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:18.920
long-held dream of doing business 
without any initial costs,

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:23.720
but in reality, doing anything without 
incurring costs is next to impossible!

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:28.290
We've been able to obtain an animation desk 
and fans from the school for free,

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.730
but even those aren't usable 
without additional elbow grease.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:33.660
The greatest example of which 
is this decrepit club room!

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:37.960
To wit: if we do not repair the 
holes in the walls and roof,

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.860
our crucial equipment runs 
the risk of water damage—

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.720
That's a alpine black swallowtail!

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:43.610
Catch it!

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:45.050
Wow, a butterfly!

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:49.620
Butterfly, flutter butter fly fly!

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.620
I have to say, the two of you are doing 
an incredible job of staying serious.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:56.850
Uh... at this point I'd like 
to remind you all that we,

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:59.630
previously, came upon the 
sizable sum of 30,000 yen!

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.130
We did!

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.950
The footage of my fall from the second floor

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:06.830
managed to sell for 30,000 
as accident footage.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:09.640
And if you'll look here, this is 
all that remains of those 30,000.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:13.260
It has been nearly exhausted in 
service of the roof and wall repairs.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.390
A moment of silence for our 
late comrade, the 30,000 yen!

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:17.400
Silence!

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.720
<i>Dearly departed 30,000 yen, 
please send a large group</i>

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.440
<i>of your comrades to my pocket.</i>

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:25.110
<i>I guess 30,000 yen is a lot of money?</i>

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:28.180
<i>That's about as much as I got for 
allowance when I was in third grade.</i>

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.250
Raccoon dog!

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.570
Row row woof, it's a raccoon dog!

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:33.570
It's a sign!

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.190
Asakusa, we should start 
a festival! It'd be great!

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.860
Row row woof, it's a raccoon dog!

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:38.500
Get serious!

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.460
We are finishing these repairs today!

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:45.070
Any idiot who wastes further time

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:48.430
will be punished without mercy,
 so keep that in mind!

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:51.270
R-Roger that.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:56.270
<b>Film</b>

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:56.270
Well, I'll handle the external holes, 
so the inside's all yours, Kanamori.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.980
Please take this seriously, Asakusa.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.010
But of course!

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:04.070
I have my doubts about that.

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:10.830
You say that, but Asakusa is pretty cool.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:14.760
Gross. What brought that on? And how, exactly?

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:19.490
I have a big problem with people who 
start a conversation by praising someone.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.180
That sounds like you!

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:24.830
But repairing the walls 
seems like a lot of work.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.760
Isn't it impressive that 
she volunteered to do it?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.330
She's only doing it because she wants to.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.650
Asakusa is self-interested in that way.

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:34.540
You mean she enjoys helping people?

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:38.690
She isn't considering the fact 
that the work might be difficult.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:41.980
Getting to play with a drill is fun to her,
 and that gets her motivated.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.970
So it's more like our interests aligned!

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:45.740
That what she's like.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.650
Think about grade school. 
One student always rushed to

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:49.690
the broom closet when clean-up time came.

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.990
They didn't really want to help clean.

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.940
They wanted to play with 
the coolest-looking broom.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.090
That's a great example!

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:06.070
<i>I guess there wouldn't be any 
motor noise, since space is a vacuum.</i>

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:07.990
<i>The effects make for a stronger impact,</i>

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:10.260
<i>but I think I'll deliberately 
go with muted sound.</i>

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:13.760
<i>There!</i>

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:19.980
<i>Would liquid paint float off 
before actually drying in space?</i>

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:25.480
<i>That calls for electrostatic powder coating!</i>

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:26.410
<i>Hang on...</i>

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:30.440
<i>In a vacuum with no gravity, wouldn't the
 ship develop an electric charge?</i>

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:32.870
<i>Will a regular electrostatic charge be 
enough for the powder to coat properly?</i>

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:35.530
<i>Ah, who cares, it's my fantasy!</i>

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:38.150
<i>No big deal if it's a little 
bit more convenient for me.</i>

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:40.460
<i>That just leaves applying the heat.</i>

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:47.470
Care to explain why you're doodling and
 wearing a worn-out bucket on your head?

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:49.630
Uh, well...

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:52.760
I was just imagining what it'd be like 
to train to repair a spaceship.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:55.370
A spaceship?! That sounds like a ton of fun!

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:57.540
I figured as much.

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:01.480
The walls can wait for now, so could 
you at least take care of the roof?

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.480
<b>Film</b>

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.980
What do you have your bag?

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:08.260
It's a manned maneuvering unit!

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.700
I'm going, too!

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:19.750
There we go.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:35.800
This is so high up! Awesome!

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:45.270
Wow, the hole is huge up close.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:51.780
It's set. Do you think you'll 
be able to close the hole?

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:54.330
It's just sticking another 
panel over it! Piece of cake!

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:56.390
No accidents, please.

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:00.150
Let's commence the mission 
to repair the spaceship.

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:01.270
I copy!

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:02.890
Ta-dah!

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.060
<b>Club Room Ship Layout
 Eizouken</b>

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.060
<b>Mess Hall</b>

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.060
<b>Rear Hatch</b>

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.060
<b>Observation Room
Not the bridge.</b>

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.060
<b>Captain's
 cabin</b>

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.060
<b>Beds</b>

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.060
<b>Extra-large rangefinder
Not engines.</b>

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.060
<b>Antenna, not 
aerodynamic wings</b>

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.060
<b>The lens changes state from liquid
 to solid instantaneously,
 extending the range
 of the telescope</b>

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.060
<b>Ship's Hull
Since it's a medium-sized 
 space-faring vessel, it can't
 fly in high atmospheric pressure
 or high gravity, and it also can't
 withstand atmospheric entry.
 Designed with typical vertical
orientation, but because gravity
 control is a pricier option, it'll
 be operated in zero gravity.</b>

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.060
<b>A ramen bowl developed with the
 intent of making ramen slurpable
 even in zero gravity.</b>

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.060
<b>The scientific community spent 10 years 
and 12 billion dollars to develop this bowl 
which rectifies the issue. (79,8000 yen)</b>

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:04.630
The Eizouken's Club Room Ship!

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:07.650
The hull! Since it's a medium-sized
 space-faring vessel,

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:09.980
it can't fly in high atmospheric 
pressure or high gravity,

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:11.650
and it also can't withstand 
atmospheric entry.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:12.960
It uses typical vertical orientation,

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:16.130
but since gravity control is a pricier option,

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:17.690
it'll be operated in zero gravity.

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:19.020
Classical design!

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:22.170
It has a bulbous bow like you'd see in a 
maritime vessel for wave resistance,

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:25.440
but since that's pointless in space, 
we'll stick the radar in there!

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:27.880
The frame is made of a special material

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:29.530
that can transmit electrical
 and optical signals,

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.270
which eliminates the need for various cables!

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:32.980
By altering this material, you can create

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:36.820
optical and electric circuits inside of 
the frame that function like computers!

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:40.240
This is the part of the vessel that 
needs the most advanced technology!

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:43.310
And to allow for the slurping of 
ramen in zero gravity, there is—

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:43.310
Enough!

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:48.200
The hole must've been caused by a debris impact.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.670
It's pretty long.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:52.800
The impact must've been at a shallow angle.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.680
We'll use a hydraulic cutter 
to remove the warped parts.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:59.350
And here's the Pistol Grip Power Tool, 
PGT, which needs no introduction!

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:00.810
I've never heard of it before.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:04.980
Well, it's a battery-powered 
driving tool that's been

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:08.100
used since the first mission 
for the space telescope's—

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:12.930
Debris! Take cover! Now!

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.710
No way! It's hailing!

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:29.590
Yeowch!

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:43.930
The sudden rush of debris made the 
club room ship's emergency lock engage!

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:46.390
This is bad! I have to go to the bathroom!

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.380
We don't have much oxygen left.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:57.060
Hey!

00:09:57.060 --> 00:09:59.870
Mayday, mayday! Please respond!

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:02.260
Yeah, yeah, this is the command room!

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:03.690
Is it an incident or an accident?

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:06.270
An accident! The ladder fell down,
and we're stuck up here!

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:07.310
Requesting assistance!

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:09.610
I need oxygen—I mean, to use the bathroom!

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:13.070
What in the world are they doing?

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.380
Kanamori, I have to go!

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:20.090
That assistance is going to take a second.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.390
I've got a bit of situation down here, too.

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:25.390
Help me!

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:27.390
We're down to the air in our suits!

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:30.310
<i>Please! We're gonna die!</i>

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:31.740
Good grief.

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:35.330
<i>M-Mizusaki, calm down! Take deep breaths!</i>

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:41.410
<i>We're doomed!</i>

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:52.590
I'm not sure why, but please 
release the emergency lock.

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:56.230
We've got two astronauts on the 
verge of bladder rupture. Over.

00:10:57.660 --> 00:10:58.720
Or alternatively...

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:17.780
All right, the ladder is up! Now get down here!

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:20.350
K-Kanamori...

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:24.560
The bathroom emergency is taken care—

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:25.750
How'd you get down?

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:27.720
We slid down the gutter pipe—

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:30.320
I ended up having to smash through a wall.

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:35.210
That's extra labor and expenses,
which I assure you will come at a cost.

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:40.330
This rescue costs a week's worth of 
bottled milk from the Ongyoku Bathhouse.

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:42.090
S-Seven hundred yen, huh...

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:45.310
Fourteen hundred yen, actually.
I intend to drink two a day.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:45.970
<b>Film</b>

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:49.090
All right!

00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:51.540
Now to make a name for ourselves, 
so we can get promoted to club status!

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:53.190
How are we going to do that?

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:56.690
Well, we're the film club, so the 
smart thing to do would be to

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.810
produce something high quality 
to make our case to the school.

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:00.030
Heavy...

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:01.970
So heavy.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:07.650
And here I thought being a club advisor 
would be good for my circulation,

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:09.980
but my beard feels heavy, as usual.

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:11.910
Oh, and here.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:17.420
<b>Budget Deliberation Committee</b>

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:14.960
The seasonal budgets for clubs and associations

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:17.420
are based on the presentations given here.

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:19.590
Well, good luck with that.

00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:23.570
Let's announce a project 
at that with our presentation.

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:25.390
If we succeed, we'll have 
made a name for ourselves,

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:28.370
gotten promoted to a club, 
and secured a budget!

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:30.220
It'll be three birds with one stone!

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.150
It's time to go on the attack!

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:33.710
Yeah!

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:41.500
It's essentially a place to announce 
plans to the student council and teachers.

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:42.610
<b>Shibahama Food</b>

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:42.610
<b>Today's
 special</b>

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:42.610
Here's your beef bowl!

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:45.310
I'll take a shoyu ramen with 
with extra seaweed and nori!

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:50.010
The format has each team make their 
presentation in the gymnasium,

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:54.470
which is then the basis for 
their budget during that period.

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:57.380
Here's your shoyu ramen with 
extra seaweed and nori!

00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:01.880
Two bottles of milk, seven croquettes, 
and one red bean bun with smooth paste.

00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:03.860
Wait, we've gotta go up in front of a crowd?

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:05.020
That's right.

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:08.850
Each group has ten minutes 
to make their presentation.

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:13.260
Our film production association is 
going to be requesting 60,000 yen.

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:16.310
That's the maximum amount an 
"association" can ask for.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:18.500
So the anime should be about five minutes long?

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.610
We'll have to start with a 
script and some storyboards.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.780
Quality isn't our prime concern here.

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:25.800
We need to make a big impact
 with the least effort possible.

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:28.850
Our goal is to overwhelm the 
committee and secure funding,

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:31.080
along with a promotion to club status.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:34.460
Aw, I wanna take the time to make something good.

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:38.370
Easily said, but we only 
have 55 days to finish it.

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:40.610
If we go for 12 frames a second,

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.790
a five minute film means you'd 
need to produce 3600 drawings.

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:44.920
Factor in additional work beyond animation,

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:49.050
and the two of you would need to work 
50 days in a row non-stop, without sleep.

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:53.380
That being the case, we need 
to begin as soon as possible.

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:57.540
Let's... make the runtime... 
three minutes, then.

00:13:57.540 --> 00:14:00.480
We can't get started if we don't have 
any idea what the story is, though.

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:04.870
I've got a bunch of ideas
stockpiled over at my place.

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:16.540
End seat is first come, first serve!

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:19.490
Well, I get to sit on the end on the way back!

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:22.910
This is my trip home anyway, 
so no rematch for you!

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:24.270
Dang it!

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:34.310
<b>In Association with Tsubame Mizusaki</b>

00:14:35.510 --> 00:14:36.530
Huh.

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:45.090
I think the car's been hijacked 
by ads starring you, Mizusaki.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:47.860
They definitely give off a 
different impression.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:50.740
Can we shake your hand?

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:51.930
Of course.

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:53.550
Thank you so much!

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:55.410
You're very welcome.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.410
<i>She's switched into popular model mode.</i>

00:14:55.780 --> 00:14:58.410
We're big fans! Please, keep up the great work!

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:03.270
<b>Shibahama South Building</b>

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:02.420
This place is pretty neat!

00:15:05.650 --> 00:15:07.010
M'home.

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:12.430
Gimme one sec.

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:19.650
Here we go.

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:32.410
Well, that's certainly detailed.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:34.610
I looks like it'd be a lot of work to draw.

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:47.030
Let's avoid anything too complicated.

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:52.610
<b>Exit</b>

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:02.440
I like this one. It's relatively simple.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:04.570
It's basically just a stack of cubes, after all.

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:10.150
Are we fine with using this for the location?

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:13.320
I like it! So, what's going to happen here?

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:15.780
We just need the animation.

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:23.510
Tank coming through!

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:26.870
Compact frame!

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:29.930
Two main guns!

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:33.940
And it comes with flashy 
hydropneumatic suspension!

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:36.650
Is that flashy?

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:38.810
To her? Most likely.

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:41.840
Ta-dah! The personal defense tank!

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.620
<b>APFSDS
Armor-piercing
 fin-stabilized
 discarding sabot</b>

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.620
<b>HEAT
High-explosive
 anti-tank
 ammunition</b>

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.620
<b>Armor-Piercing
 Round</b>

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.620
<b>Gun-launched
 anti-tank missile</b>

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.620
<b>A trusty, fully-equipped vehicle 
which provides consistent 
support for our adventures!</b>

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.620
<b>Uses an odd caliber 
of 16.873cm.
 Has both rifled and
 smoothbore barrels. 
Length 300mm.</b>

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.620
<b>Able to jump up
 to 1m vertically</b>

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.620
<b>High-end 
hydropneumatic
 suspension makes
 low riders you'd
 see in the streets
 seem like kids' stuff.</b>

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.620
<b>Continuous tracks result in
 zero relative speed with
 the point of contact, which is cool!</b>

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.620
<b>Reaches speeds of 190 kmph,
 even on rough terrain.</b>

00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:44.140
An older design that resembles a rice cake.

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:45.480
It's cool how using continuous tracks

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:48.820
results in zero relative speed 
difference with the point of contact!

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:52.110
It can hit 190 km/h,
 even over rough terrain!

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:57.410
A trusty, fully-equipped vehicle which provides 
consistent support for our adventures!

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.530
The turret knocks the entire 
turret rig backwards

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:07.330
to eject the shell casing, 
after which it sits back up!

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.680
The sound's a bit out of sync.

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:25.820
That's detail in the sound effects.

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:28.250
Light travels faster than sound, y'know.

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:28.890
Think about light—

00:17:28.890 --> 00:17:30.180
Okay, enough.

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:33.690
This is great and all, but can
 you draw it, Mizusaki?

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.770
Well, I've never done effects

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:39.700
like smoke and fire before, 
so I'd have to try first.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:43.700
But the kind of animation 
I want to make is more like...

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.410
Sliding down an incline—

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:54.660
And falling!

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:56.550
Too plain.

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:02.810
You know that some animation 
puts a focus on realism, right?

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:05.180
It can be really ordinary, everyday actions...

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:08.060
But when animated, it looks really amazing!

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:10.020
Isn't there something more efficient?

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.710
Some kind of animation spectacle that

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:14.500
would be impressive to anyone who's watching?

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:18.490
To me, this is the most 
spectacular animation there is!

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:20.970
It'd cost too much for how plain it is!

00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:23.090
You can even use limited animation, but please,

00:18:23.090 --> 00:18:25.370
make something that's more flashy!

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.990
Animation is supposed to be about motion,

00:18:29.990 --> 00:18:34.500
and animators are supposed 
to make stuff move!

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:37.300
—make stuff move!

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:39.990
Y'know, some professional 
animators will pick up a sword

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:42.150
and swing it around while working.

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:45.160
<b>Summer Anime Special</b>

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:45.160
<b>How It's Made!</b>

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:48.540
<b>Part 3: Attention to Detail in Animation</b>

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:56.190
What kind of poses happen when 
you've got a sword on your hip?

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:58.150
How does it look when you unsheathe it?

00:18:58.150 --> 00:19:00.150
How do the wrinkles bunch up
 when you move in a hakama?

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:04.160
They work while studying all 
those details, not just imagining them!

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:09.010
Being an animator is like being an actor!

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:11.680
But you portray more than just people...

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:14.980
The movement of dogs and cats, 
the ocean, the weather...

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:18.920
Cars, planes, all of that 
is the animators acting!

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:23.130
I want to draw realistic, 
lifelike acting with my own hands!

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:28.180
I don't just want to make anime, 
I want to make animation!

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:34.260
—to make animation!

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:31.980
<i>It won't matter how flashy 
the subject matter is</i>

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:34.410
<i>if the final product has 
less motion than a picture book.</i>

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:36.650
<i>That won't make a good impression
 with the review committee.</i>

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.820
<i>Technical experience 
is valuable, but more than that,</i>

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:42.110
<i>hurting the artist's motivation seems unwise.</i>

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:48.660
Fair enough. Let's combine the tank 
with what you're trying to do, Mizusaki.

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:53.250
How about a schoolgirl with a 
sword fighting a tank?!

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:57.380
You can put the focus on realistic 
acting with the girl's animation!

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:59.220
Oh... okay.

00:19:59.650 --> 00:20:02.250
And we can balance that by 
making the parts with the tank

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:04.180
and the explosions as over-the-top as we can.

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:08.950
Sounds good to me!

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:34.750
Should the sword be a katana?

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:36.470
How about a machete?

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:37.950
It's a bit more realistic for combat,

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:40.180
and you see them in action movies all the time,

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:43.730
but not too much in anime, I think!

00:20:43.730 --> 00:20:46.260
I like the realism! Let's go with that!

00:20:50.590 --> 00:20:52.790
Her hair should be able to flutter in the wind.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:58.590
So cool!

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:02.260
Maybe I'm missing something, but how's 
she going to be able to fight a tank?

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:06.770
What if we give her an oxygen tank and mask?

00:21:06.770 --> 00:21:07.490
Huh?

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:09.540
The world she's on has low gravity!

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:13.010
Which means the atmosphere is thin, 
and you need the mask to breathe!

00:21:13.010 --> 00:21:15.930
But in exchange, since she came 
from a world with stronger gravity,

00:21:15.930 --> 00:21:18.310
she can jump around all over 
the place, really quickly!

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:20.470
Since you won't have to worry about the face,

00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:22.300
you can put your focus on the action!

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:25.010
Faces take quite a bit of time, after all.

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:26.840
I wanted to draw expressions, too.

00:21:27.170 --> 00:21:29.890
Then how about simplifying 
things for the long shots,

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:33.620
but then you go for detail 
during the close ups?

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:35.590
Yeah! That should work!

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:38.310
Okay! Let's do that!

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:40.210
You're getting fired up!

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:43.320
<i>I can't believe that animation 
paper costs so much,</i>

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:44.900
<i>when the only thing 
special about it is the holes.</i>

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:48.110
<i>Wouldn't punching holes in 
regular paper be good enough?</i>

00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:51.020
<i>Hello... a hole puncher for animation pegs?</i>

00:21:51.020 --> 00:21:55.470
<i>It's the exact three holes needed... 
this'll cover its own cost in no time.</i>

00:22:03.470 --> 00:22:06.090
So one thing we can do to make things 
look flashy without extra work

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:08.050
is draw one explosion,

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:12.780
and then copy it, to make it 
look like a string of blasts.

00:22:14.990 --> 00:22:16.310
I see.

00:22:16.310 --> 00:22:19.310
Oh, there's that thing where you build up
 tension during a big attack...

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:21.310
Cut between the tank, the girl,
 the tank, and the girl,

00:22:21.310 --> 00:22:23.320
enough that it starts to seem repetitive!

00:22:26.690 --> 00:22:28.820
Ta-dah! A vast world!

00:22:29.410 --> 00:22:30.950
A girl in a gas mask!

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:32.330
And her foe...

00:22:52.650 --> 00:22:54.980
Wouldn't it be easy to shoot 
someone who's jumping around?

00:22:55.910 --> 00:22:57.410
We can give her a cable gun, then.

00:22:59.570 --> 00:23:02.770
And then, while firing 
the cable, she climbs up a wall!

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:05.920
All to get in the blind spot of the tank,

00:23:05.920 --> 00:23:07.970
since its turret can't aim high enough!

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:14.700
But then!

00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:26.000
Will it all work out in the end?!

00:23:26.310 --> 00:23:28.230
Dun dun...

00:24:55.970 --> 00:25:00.250
<b>Illustration by: Tsukumizu</b>
